# Comment style (ysk.bel)

Explanatory comments are for **maintainers and editors**. User-facing strings stay whatever language the site needs; **the comment itself is English**.

**Scope:** the **whole repository** — any file kind that can carry comments (JS/SCSS/Liquid `{% comment %}`, config, Markdown, YAML, shells, …).

## Write comments when

- Behaviour or **contracts** are not obvious from names (variants, toggles, cross-file wiring).
- Editors must **sync** values across files (phone, anchors, carousel order, CI env).
- There is a **browser / a11y / motion** or **build** constraint worth preserving.

## Prefer not to comment when

- The next line fully explains itself.
- The comment only **repeats identifiers** or duplicates typings.

## Shape and readability

- Use **`/** … */`**, Liquid `{% comment %}`, or aligned `*` / `#` lines so prose can wrap. **Do not cram** unrelated sentences on one long line.
- **One idea per line** after the opening summary is fine.
- Optional bullets (`•` or `-`) for variants, steps, or file lists.

## Link the glossary

- Unusual UX/publishing or shared UI terms (**scrim**, **colophon**, **prefers-reduced-motion**, **`aria-current`**, …) → **`docs/glossary.md`**, cite the heading, e.g. `docs/glossary.md («Scrim»)`.

## By kind of file

- **Data / config (JS, JSON where commented, Eleventy):** what consumes it; field contracts; **propagation** (other files to update).
- **Scripts:** **why** timing or overrides exist; **where** SCSS/tests must stay aligned.
- **Styles:** file or section opener (template + tokens + layout intent); glossary when explaining behaviour, not only a token name.
- **Liquid:** short blocks for editorial structure (banner variants, duplication rules); link glossary for colophon etc.
- **CI / tooling:** intent of non-obvious steps; avoid secrets in comments.

```js
/** GOOD — variants + linkage */
/**
 * Announcement banner (see `components/info-banner.liquid`).
 *
 * `variant`:
 *   • `strip` — under the navbar; everyday notices.
 *   • `modal` — overlay + dialog UX; rare, major news only.
 */
```

```scss
/* GOOD — glossary when behaviour matters */
/*
 * Drawer scrim — docs/glossary.md («Scrim»).
 * Below `.menu` and navbar; no transition when prefers-reduced-motion.
 */
```

## Hygiene

- Fix **grammar** in comments you touch.
- Remove **dead commented-out code** unless it documents an intentional rollback.
- No **opaque roadmap labels** (`Group B`, `P5`) unless you replace them with a stable description in the same comment.
